title: Characters, personas, and safe card import and export
---
date: 2026-10-18
---
author: Labyricorn
---
summary: Parity milestones one and two add revisioned character cards, per-conversation casts, and a transactional importer for common card formats.
---
tags: ai, interface, user-control, sqlite
---
source_commit: 8bcb70bc6da29c6c223a797bd4c14d527bd34b25
---
body:

The first two parity milestones made conversations about characters rather than
only about models.

**Characters.** Cards are revisioned, and each conversation has its own cast,
greetings, and historical speaker identity, so an old message still shows who
spoke it after a card changes. Prompts are assembled with bounded macro
expansion and a context estimate, and the stored prompt matches what was sent.

**Interchange.** An importer reads Tavern V1, V2, and V3 cards in JSON and PNG
form, CHARX archives, native cards, and a versioned Labbonet snapshot. Preview is
a real import inside a transaction that is rolled back, which yields exact counts
without a separate preview format. A stateless preview token was considered and
rejected for that reason.

Imported content is treated as inert data. Archives with executable extensions or
unsafe paths are rejected whole, unknown assets are ignored with a note, and
oversized portraits are downscaled instead of dropped. Snapshots omit
conversation parameters and provenance so a file cannot smuggle in provider
settings. Imported threads carry no endpoint or model, and a destructive reset
takes a backup first.

Some browser paths, such as the native file chooser, were not exercised in this
pass and were carried forward to the milestone audit.

[Commit 8bcb70b](https://github.com/Labyricorn/Labbonet/commit/8bcb70bc6da29c6c223a797bd4c14d527bd34b25)
